sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor U as Client (owner or agent)
  participant D as Dashboard SPA
  participant S as Edge fn save
  participant P as Edge fn publish
  participant DB as Postgres (RLS + service fns)
  participant R as Build runner (GitHub Actions)
  participant X as Edge fn export-published
  participant C as Edge fn job-callback
  participant CF as Cloudflare (site Worker)

  U->>D: edit listing, add photos
  D->>D: validateItem(draft) in the browser
  D->>S: save(...) with user JWT
  S->>DB: service.contract_for(): 404 if not a member (before any validation)
  S->>S: validateItem(draft) against that contract
  S->>DB: service.save_as(): role, own-only, locked fields
  DB-->>S: version n (site unchanged)
  U->>D: Publish
  D->>P: publish(rows) with user JWT
  P->>DB: service.contract_for(): 404 if not a member
  P->>P: validateItem(publish) on exactly the given versions: required, alt, rights, processed photos, sources
  P->>DB: service.start_publish(): job with the validated versions pinned, nothing goes live
  P->>R: repository_dispatch {job_id, site_id} (concurrency group per site, queue max)
  R->>X: export-published(job, runner key)
  X->>DB: service.published_rows(job): exactly the snapshot
  X-->>R: rows + resolved contract + site target + that site's deploy token (Vault)
  R->>R: check site id = payload site_id, place() -> render -> launch layer -> gates
  alt any gate fails
    R->>C: job-callback failed + gate report (runner signature)
    C->>DB: service.set_job_state(failed): nothing goes live
    D-->>U: "Not published: 2 photos have no alt text" (plain words)
  else all gates pass
    R->>CF: deploy to the site's own Worker with its per-site token
    R->>CF: smoke test (headers, redirects, 404, form endpoint)
    R->>C: job-callback done + deploy id
    C->>DB: service.set_job_state(done): the job's rows go live at their snapshot versions
    D-->>U: "Published" + link + history entry
  end
